---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { DialogConfirmations, DialogPlayground, DialogSearch, DialogSizes } from '../../components/DialogDemo';
import { DialogFlows, DialogStates } from '../../components/DialogFlowsDemo';
---

<Docs title="Dialog" description="Modal dialogs for confirmations, forms, file previews, and search.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Dialog</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A modal window over the page. Use it for decisions that need an answer now, short forms, previews, and search. Focus
    stays inside until it closes, then returns to where it was.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="dialog-demo">
    <DialogPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Dialog usage"
      code={`import { Button } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/button";
import {
  Dialog,
  DialogBody,
  DialogContent,
  DialogDescription,
  DialogFooter,
  DialogHeader,
  DialogTitle,
  DialogTrigger,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/dialog";

<Dialog open={open} onOpenChange={(next) => !pending && setOpen(next)}>
  <DialogTrigger render={<Button variant="destructive" size="sm" />}>
    Remove member
  </DialogTrigger>
  <DialogContent finalFocus={() => trigger.current ?? heading.current}>
    <DialogHeader>
      <DialogTitle>Remove kofi@meadow.example?</DialogTitle>
      <DialogDescription>
        They lose access to this workspace now.
      </DialogDescription>
    </DialogHeader>
    <DialogFooter>
      <Button variant="outline" disabled={pending} onClick={() => setOpen(false)}>
        Cancel
      </Button>
      <Button variant="destructive" disabled={pending} aria-busy={pending} onClick={remove}>
        {pending ? "Saving change…" : "Confirm removal"}
      </Button>
    </DialogFooter>
  </DialogContent>
</Dialog>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>Dialog</code> works controlled with <code>open</code> and <code>onOpenChange</code>, or uncontrolled with{' '}
      <code>defaultOpen</code>. To block Escape and outside clicks while work is saving, ignore the change in{' '}
      <code>onOpenChange</code>. You can also mount the dialog only while it is open.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>DialogContent</code> portals an overlay and the popup, and adds a corner close button. Turn it off with{' '}
      <code>showCloseButton={'{false}'}</code>. <code>DialogFooter showCloseButton</code> adds an outline Close button
      after your actions.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Sizes</h2>
    <p>
      <code>size</code> is <code>"default"</code> (24rem, scrolls as a whole), <code>"form"</code> (36rem, the header
      stays put and <code>DialogBody</code> scrolls), <code>"split"</code> (64rem, no padding, for two panes), or{' '}
      <code>"fullscreen"</code> (covers the viewport). Below 40rem every size fills the width minus a 1rem gutter.
    </p>
    <DialogSizes client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Confirmations</h2>
    <p>
      Pass <code>finalFocus</code> a function so focus goes back to the trigger, or to a section heading with{' '}
      <code>tabIndex={'{-1}'}</code> if the row is gone. Errors stay inside the dialog as an <code>Alert</code>, so the
      person can try again.
    </p>
    <DialogConfirmations client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">States</h2>
    <p>
      Dialogs often open before their data arrives. Show a skeleton with <code>role="status"</code>, an error with a
      retry, and an empty <code>StatePanel</code> when there is nothing to choose. Leave out the description until it
      has something to say.
    </p>
    <DialogStates client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Flows</h2>
    <p>
      The footer can hold a hint as a direct <code>&lt;p&gt;</code>, a submit button tied to a form with{' '}
      <code>form="…"</code>, or a back step. Without a footer, put actions in a right-aligned row at the end of the
      body. A second dialog can open on top; when it closes, move focus to the control the person needs next.
    </p>
    <DialogFlows client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Search</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Top placement"
      code={`<DialogContent
  data-slot="search-dialog"
  placement="top"
  showCloseButton={false}
  className="flex max-w-2xl flex-col gap-0 p-0"
>
  <DialogTitle className="sr-only">Search Meadow</DialogTitle>
  …
</DialogContent>

<DialogContent
  placement="top"
  style={{ "--sprout-dialog-top": "33.333%" }}
  className="gap-0 p-0"
  showCloseButton={false}
>
  <DialogHeader className="sr-only">…</DialogHeader>
  …
</DialogContent>`}
    />
    <DialogSearch client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="dialog-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <p>
      <code>Dialog</code>, <code>DialogTrigger</code>, <code>DialogPortal</code>, <code>DialogClose</code>,{' '}
      <code>DialogOverlay</code>, <code>DialogTitle</code>, and <code>DialogDescription</code> wrap the Base UI dialog
      parts and take their props, including <code>render</code>. <code>DialogHeader</code>, <code>DialogBody</code>, and{' '}
      <code>DialogFooter</code> render a <code>div</code> and accept <code>render</code>, so a body can be the form.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>DialogContent</code> takes <code>size</code>, <code>placement</code>(<code>"center"</code> or{' '}
      <code>"top"</code>; top reads <code>--sprout-dialog-top</code>, default 12dvh), <code>showCloseButton</code>,{' '}
      <code>closeLabel</code>, <code>container</code>, and every Base UI popup prop such as <code>initialFocus</code>{' '}
      and <code>finalFocus</code>. It sets <code>data-slot="dialog-content"</code> (overridable), <code>data-size</code>
      , and <code>data-placement</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The popup has <code>role="dialog"</code> and is named by <code>DialogTitle</code>. Every dialog needs a title,
      even if it is visually hidden with <code>sr-only</code>. Tab and Shift+Tab stay inside. Escape and outside clicks
      close it unless you ignore the change. Focus moves to the first focusable element, or to <code>initialFocus</code>
      .
    </p>
    <p>
      Opening fades and scales in over 180ms; closing takes 120ms. Both turn off when reduced motion is requested, and
      fullscreen dialogs only fade.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Dialogs use <code>--sprout-overlay</code>, <code>--sprout-surface</code>, <code>--sprout-canvas</code>,{' '}
      <code>--sprout-line</code>, <code>--sprout-text</code>, <code>--sprout-muted</code>,{' '}
      <code>--sprout-shadow-overlay</code>, and <code>--sprout-radius-panel</code>. They need no brand color, so they
      look the same with the neutral and TulipFarm themes in light and dark mode.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
